//   function, context: ffi.Pointer) -> TreeStats
// Query an AABB for overlapping proxies. The callback is called for each proxy
// that overlaps the supplied AABB. No filtering is performed. Returns
// performance data
// C: `b2TreeStats b2DynamicTree_OverlapAABBAll(const b2DynamicTree *tree,
// b2AABB aabb, function *callback, void *context)`
func m.dynamic_tree_overlap_aabb_all(tree, aabb, callback, context){}

// dynamic_tree_cast_ray(tree: ffi.Pointer, input: RayCastInput, mask_bits: int,
//   callback: function, context: ffi.Pointer) -> TreeStats
// Ray cast against the proxies in the tree. This relies on the callback to
// perform an exact ray cast in the case where the proxy contains a shape. The
// callback also performs any collision filtering. This has performance roughly
// equal to k * log(n), where k is the number of collisions and n is the number
// of proxies in the tree. Bit-wise filtering using mask bits can improve
// performance in some scenarios. However, this filtering may be approximate, so
// the user should still apply filtering to results. Returns performance data
// C: `b2TreeStats b2DynamicTree_CastRay(const b2DynamicTree *tree, const
// b2RayCastInput *input, uint64_t maskBits, function *callback, void *context)`
// [tree]: the dynamic tree to ray cast
// [input]: the ray cast input data.
// [mask_bits]: mask bits used to filter proxies.
// [callback]: a callback that is called for each proxy that is hit by the ray
// [context]: user context that is passed to the callback
func m.dynamic_tree_cast_ray(tree, input, mask_bits, callback, context){}

// dynamic_tree_cast_box(tree: ffi.Pointer, input: BoxCastInput, mask_bits: int,
//   callback: function, context: ffi.Pointer) -> TreeStats
// Cast a swept AABB through the tree. This has performance roughly equal to k *
// log(n), where k is the number of collisions and n is the number of proxies in
// the tree. Returns performance data
// C: `b2TreeStats b2DynamicTree_CastBox(const b2DynamicTree *tree, const
// b2BoxCastInput *input, uint64_t maskBits, function *callback, void *context)`
// [tree]: the dynamic tree to cast through
// [input]: the AABB cast input. The box sweeps from its origin to origin +
//   maxFraction * translation.
// [mask_bits]: filter bits: `bool accept = (maskBits & proxy->categoryBits) !=
//   0;`
// [callback]: a callback that is called for each proxy the swept box may hit
// [context]: user context that is passed to the callback
func m.dynamic_tree_cast_box(tree, input, mask_bits, callback, context){}

